transcription path under \\\"Fabrication reads as plausible, not as wrong\\\".\\n\\nNote on scope: the originating research entry named `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md`, but that file is the orchestrator (mode routing, relay rules, post-actions) and holds no tool list. The gap lands on the agent file it spawns.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n```\\ngit grep -in \\\"crawl\\\\|structured extraction\\\\|local cache\\\\|vector\\\" -- \\\\\\n  .claude/agents/research-curator.md .claude/skills/research-curator/\\n\u2192 1 match, unrelated: references/extraction-methodology.md:148\\n  (a term-pairing example listing `vector` as a search synonym)\\n\\ngit grep -n \\\"WebFetch\\\\|WebSearch\\\\|ref_search_documentation\\\\|ctx_fetch_and_index\\\" -- \\\\\\n  .claude/agents/research-curator.md .claude/skills/research-curator/\\n\u2192 3 matches, all in the search/read family\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSurfaced by `research-insight-extractor` while processing `research/mcp-ecosystem/wigolo.md` (PR #3788). Confidence: High. Impact: Low.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Correction To The Original Capture S Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe capture recorded `git grep -il \\\"wigolo\\\" -- .` \u2192 1 match (`research/README.md`) as confirming no existing wiring. That count is now 9: the same run's cross-reference reciprocity pass added 8 backlink table rows to peer `research/mcp-ecosystem/` entries. Those 8 are Cross-Reference rows, not tool wiring, so the \\\"no existing wiring\\\" conclusion is unchanged \u2014 only the count was stale.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Note On Original Capture\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis item was captured by `backlog_add` into the local cache under reference `p2-research-curator-agents-tool-list-offers-no-crawl-or-structu`, but GitHub issue creation failed at the time with `403 GitHub GraphQL is not available from Claude Code sessions`, leaving `item_ref` empty. This issue is that capture, written through the GitHub MCP instead.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"dad4448ecc6beab6f7777c05d4c37c767009077b6bc2cb355dd39c685f8175a4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCElvA\"}"}